      "title": "Troubleshooting HTTP 502/504 and DNS Failures in Config Manager via Proxy",
      "content_summary": "Addresses connectivity issues in Config Manager where proxy configurations lead to DNS lookup failures and HTTP 502/504 errors, often caused by network or firewall misconfigurations.",
      "content_body": "When Config Manager returns HTTP 502 or 504 errors alongside DNS lookup failures, first verify that the proxy exclusion list includes the necessary Config Manager endpoints. Incorrect network configuration, specifically missing or malformed proxy bypass entries, is a common root cause. Ensure that firewall rules allow outbound traffic on the required ports from the Config Manager server to external update services. Updating firewall rules to permit these specific connections and correcting the DNS resolution path typically resolves the issue. Check the Config Manager log files for specific proxy timeout codes to confirm if the traffic is being blocked at the network layer."
